WEBVTT

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.240
Why is something like that...

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.160
Fried Potato!

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:17.920
Transistor!

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.520
Taiyaki!

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:26.360
Taiyaki? What's up with pickin' nothin' but food all this time?

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.190
What's wrong with it?

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.040
Well, not that I really care...

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.440
The 'ki' from Taiyaki!

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.020
'ki'...

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:36.370
'ki'?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.820
I did it, I did it!

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.240
Ouch!

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.530
Let's switch for a while.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.640
Kaoru! But I'm fine.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.140
Really.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.830
It's mysterious.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.680
The sea at night, I mean.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.910
It looks very quiet...

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.080
...but...

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.610
...there's something frightening
about it that can't be explained.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.040
Did something happen on that island?

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.870
What do you mean, all of a sudden?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.110
Did you think we hadn't realized?

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.780
Tell me... what happened.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.030
I see.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.280
The blisters and the cut...

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.490
Don't worry.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.210
I don't think it's anything serious.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.860
Maybe the cut wasn't as deep as I had thought.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.670
It might be Nanomachines.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:00.110
Do you remember?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.720
That giant crab that was protecting the ruins.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:06.710
Yes...

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.730
That crab was being controlled by Nanomachines.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.320
It's possible...

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:18.780
...that Nanomachines got into your body in one form or another.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.810
Into my body?

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.590
I heard at the training school...

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:31.570
...that Nanomachines that are injected into the body and repair injuries were being developed.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.510
I think you'd best have Chako look into it.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.620
Something like that actually exists?

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.040
Hey, Shingo...

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.740
Well, I can't say for sure that they don't...

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.410
How is it?

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.270
Yep. No doubt about it.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.460
There's Nanomachines in Luna's body.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.120
Then the reason her cut healed in one day...

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:23.210
Just like Kaoru said, probably
because of the Nanomachines.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:24.820
Really.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.640
So there really are Nanomachines in my body...

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.510
But why is something like that in Luna's body?

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:40.310
I dunno. Either they got in on their own, or somebody put 'em in Luna for some reason.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:45.820
Are these Nanomachines like the Nano-Plants that were in the giant crab?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:50.390
They're similarly independant, but not so mechanical.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:56.360
Tiny Nanomachines are spread throughout Luna's body like a virus.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:00.030
While we're here, should I check you all out too?

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.560
Howard!

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.990
Right, that's the lot of you.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:17.620
The result of the examination is that only Luna and Adam showed a reaction.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.740
I see!

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.690
So that's how it was!

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:23.690
What's this that that was how?

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:28.420
I don't know, but it's the secret of Luna and Adam being able to communicate.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.130
The secret of us being able to communicate?

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:37.160
Remember when we fought those three?

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:42.670
Back then, the giant crab responded to Adam's feelings and came to our rescue, right?

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.140
I'm sure the Nanomachines have a sensor or something that senses Adam's feelings.

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:53.090
So you're saying that Luna's feelings are communicated to Adam via this sensor as well?

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.530
It's quite possible.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:08:00.030
There's a sensor in my body for how Adam is feeling?

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:01.380
Luna...

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:08.360
It's possible that's also the reason only Luna could hear that voice.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:12.630
And also opening the door to the ruins--it was all because of the Nanomachines.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:15.070
So you mean it was for Adam's sake?

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:21.410
But these Nanomachines are probably run-of-the-mill for Adam's people.

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:23.170
Will Luna be okay?

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:25.160
I don't know that either.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:28.870
Although there doesn't seem to be anythin' wrong with her body right now.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:30.590
Luna...

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.030
It's okay, Adam.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.660
And the rest of you, don't make those faces either.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:39.410
Chako said there's nothing wrong with my body, didn't she?

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:46.340
And isn't it great that I have Nanomachines in my body that fix my injuries all on their own?

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:52.760
I feel relieved. If I'd known this is all it would be, I'd have asked Chako to check it out sooner.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:56.430
Now let's all take our stations and give our best again today!

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:58.380
It's only a little further to the mainland!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.260
So...

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.740
My duty today is... food, right?

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.190
Alright! I'll make some super-delicious food, so look forward to it!

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:11.690
She's forcing it.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:12.930
Luna...

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.560
Why me?

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:31.460
What's... going to happen to me?

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.730
Chako, how was Luna?

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.840
As usual, spaced out.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:45.560
I see...

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:50.580
It's already been three days since then. Whatever she says, she's definitely uneasy.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.910
It's okay, Adam.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:57.480
Luna will be fine. Do you think she'd lose to Nanomachines?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.990
Ain't there anythin' we can do that would "Pow!" make Luna cheerful again?

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:12.820
Have a party?

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:15.820
We want to get Luna cheerful again.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.320
She acts cheerful in front of us, but she's definitely uneasy!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:25.610
Well of course. She just found out something inexplicable is in her body.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:30.220
Luna's shift is in the evening, so she'll probably stay in the bedroom all day.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.390
So in the meanwhile we can get things ready and surprise Luna!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.690
A party... sounds like fun!

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.340
Let's do it! I'm in favour!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.920
If it'll make Luna happy again, I have nothing against it.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.190
And Menori?

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:47.470
Fine by me.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:51.670
When you think about it, Luna's always been cheering all of us up.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.930
Alright! It's decided!

00:10:55.120 --> 00:11:00.480
Right! Now that that's decided, I'll catch a super big fish to be the main dish!

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:05.470
So we'll leave fishin' to Howard, and the rest of us'll prepare the party site!

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:27.140
...despite which, I haven't caught a thing.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:29.880
Like that, like that!

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:31.910
Lookin' good!

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.070
This should do it!

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:36.220
Looks like the party site preparations are done.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:37.490
Yes!

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:39.480
We did it!

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.240
Woo-hoo!

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.410
We're okay over here.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.210
How're you doin'?

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.210
Completely hopeless.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:54.670
No matter how good my skills are, if there aren't fish, I can't catch them.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:58.380
It was a mistake to leave it to Howard.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.260
Got one?

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.130
This is a biggie!

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.940
What'cha doin'? Pull it in!

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.780
I know that much without you telling me!

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:18.180
What's a "biggie"? I've never seen one that small!

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.270
What happened?

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:56.470
Howard...

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:59.130
Idiot, let go! Let go!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.230
Howard! It'll pull you out!

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.530
Shut up! As though I'd give up on a fish this big!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.440
Howard!

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:12.630
Damn it!

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.630
Howard!

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:18.520
Kaoru! Kaoru! Stop the ship immediately!

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:19.980
It's an emergency!

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:32.170
It's Howard!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.370
What a relief!

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:34.490
How's Howard?

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:35.660
Right over there.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.230
Oh no!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.340
Huh? What?

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.570
Papa!

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.690
What happened? Where's Howard?

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:10.270
I'm sure he's fine.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:11.510
There he is!

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:16.190
Howard!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.820
Help me!

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:32.660
Kaoru...

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.280
I'm saved.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:46.230
Howard!

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:49.010
Howard, that was brave!

00:14:58.570 --> 00:14:59.690
Did something happen?

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.240
It seems like the ship has stopped.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.860
No, it's nothing.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.260
You have night shift today.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.680
You should sleep a little longer.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.680
Thanks.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.710
I really thought I was done for!

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.520
But this is perfect for the main dish!

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:23.810
Well, let's let Shingo and Adam take care'a cookin' and start rehearsal.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:27.740
Rehearsal?

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.320
We're doing something like <i>that</i>?

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:36.860
If we were just eatin' it wouldn't be all that much fun.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.390
Well be that as it may...

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.320
Let's do it! It sounds like fun!

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:43.420
I'll do it! For Luna!

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:44.920
There's Bell for ya.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.680
Further proof we're all friends!

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.590
Please, Menori?

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.360
I guess I must.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.530
But just this once!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.170
Then let's get practicing!

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:08.810
Kaoru, it's almost time.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.430
Switch it onto autopilot, and let's go.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.020
Luna...

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:15.930
Luna?

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:18.860
Sorry, but it's almost time for your shift.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.470
We're countin' on ya.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.380
I know. I'll be up in a second.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:23.840
Alright!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.220
Huh?

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.610
What is this?

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.230
A surprise party!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.040
It's okay to have on once in a while, right?

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.330
You're the guest of honour today.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:44.390
I am?

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:47.960
For always doing your best as the leader.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.840
Wow.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:59.660
Well, let's enjoy it!

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:07.870
Too much!

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.380
Then maybe I'll take a few!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.710
And it had a mouth like this!

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:43.310
That was delicious!

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:46.530
It's been a while since we had food that good!

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.560
Thanks, everyone.

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:50.990
I guess it's time we got started.

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:51.740
Got that right.

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:52.720
"Started"?

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:56.360
C'mon. The guest of honour should sit.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:58.010
What's going to start?

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.810
You'll just have to look forward to seeing it.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.580
And now, today's main event...

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:15.370
"The Fairy of the Flower Garden," written by Sharla and directed by Chako, will begin!

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.030
"The Fairy of the Flower Garden"?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.430
Once upon a time in a far off land...

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.620
...there lived a girl who loved flowers.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:31.010
Ah! There's a beautiful flower patch in such a place!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.410
Howard?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.170
Lookin' good, Howard!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:36.710
Cute!

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:39.480
Over here, and over there!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:40.830
Huh?

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.970
What a beautiful one!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.120
A pretty obvious choice, huh?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.070
Yeah...

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:52.980
Before she noticed, the girl was lost in the flower garden.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.960
Huh? I wonder where I am.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:58.530
A flower garden?

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.290
Who cares about a flower patch?

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.480
I'll kill these while you watch!

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.580
Stop! The flowers...

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.840
Someone! Save the flowers!

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.640
Stop it!

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:16.340
Who might you be?

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.740
I am the Flower Spirit!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.560
I came when I heard your call.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.920
Leave the rest to me.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.380
Now, a duel!

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:27.710
Sounds fun.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.920
I'll be your opponent!

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.830
Go! Menori!

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:35.320
Go for it, Bell!

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:41.510
What's wrong, what's wrong, Flower Spirit?

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:50.660
You got me!

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:51.260
Great!

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:53.470
Thank you, flower spirit.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.680
I should be the one to thank you.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:02.130
Thank you for inforing me of the threat to the flower garden.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:05.920
Is there any wish I can grant you in thanks?

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:06.630
Adam...
Is there any wish I can grant you in thanks?

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:06.820
Adam...

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:08.810
A wish?

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:09.670
Yes.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.010
This next bit is what'cha gotta see!

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:19.310
I'd like to see this flower patch from above, even if just once!

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:23.240
That's a simple matter.

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:26.240
Now, hold on tight to me.

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:27.330
I shall!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.280
Now, let's go!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:31.040
To the sky!

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:32.280
Go!

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.830
I'm flying! I'm really flying!

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:02.430
And thus, the flower garden was protected.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:07.120
Everyone...

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.330
Thank you.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.630
I...

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:20.470
Thanks, everyone. I won't give up!

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:22.310
No matter what happens.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.130
Yeah, yeah! <i>That's</i> our Luna!

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.790
Who cares about Nanomachines?

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:31.010
We'll always be together.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:38.360
Luna...

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.320
Adam, I'm sorry for worrying you.

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:06.520
Ah! There's a beautiful flower patch in such a place!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.570
Over here, and over there...

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:14.660
Ouch...

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:24.820
Wake up! Wake up! Everyone, wake up!

00:22:26.540 --> 00:22:29.170
What's wrong? It's awfully early!

00:22:29.170 --> 00:22:31.610
Look! Look out front!

00:22:33.860 --> 00:22:36.860
Look, everyone. Take a good look.

00:22:46.830 --> 00:22:49.490
We've finally... arrived.

00:22:52.230 --> 00:22:56.990
Land ho! Land ho!

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:07.040
Woo-hoo! We've arrived on the mainland!

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:10.380
Everyone's really happy to see terra firma for the first time in a while.

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:14.320
But Luna's lookin' depressed for some reason.

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:19.190
Bell, bein' Bell, worries and worries, but it looks like there's nothin' we can do!

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:23.880
It gives me a sense like somethin's gonna happen!

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:28.230
Next time: Finally arrived.
